   "source": [
    "# NumCompute Quickstart: Student Performance Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates the NumCompute toolkit using the supplied `numcompute_student_performance.csv` dataset. It is written with **Python's standard library and NumPy only**; it does not use pandas, scikit-learn, or other data/ML libraries.\n",
    "\n",
    "The examples cover:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Reading a mixed-type CSV and a numeric view with missing values.\n",
    "2. Imputation, standardisation, one-hot encoding, and a preprocessing pipeline.\n",
    "3. Stable sorting, multi-key sorting, top-k, quickselect, and binary search.\n",
    "4. Tie-aware ranking, percentiles, descriptive statistics, histograms, and streaming Welford statistics.\n",
    "5. Classification/regression metrics, ROC/AUC, numerical gradients and a Jacobian.\n",
    "6. A reproducible loop-versus-vectorised benchmark with environment details.\n",
    "\n",
    "**How to run:** open the project root in VS Code/Jupyter and run the cells from top to bottom. The CSV is bundled at `demo/data/numcompute_student_performance.csv`. If you move this notebook, keep the CSV at that relative location or update `DATA_PATH` in the next cell."
   ]
  },
